[Chapter "Main line (4.Nc3 dxc4)"]
[Line "Gambit: 5.e4"]
[Opening "Slav Defense: Geller Gambit"]

{White gives up the c4 pawn for a big centre. Black keeps it and finds a strong square for the knight.} 1. d4 d5 {Claim the centre.} 2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit: White attacks d5.} 2... c6 {The Slav: support d5 with a pawn and keep the c8 bishop's diagonal open, unlike ...e6.} 3. Nf3 Nf6 {Develop and guard d5 again.} 4. Nc3 dxc4 {Take on c4. White will win the pawn back, but meanwhile Black gets ...Bf5 in.} 5. e4 {A gambit: White doesn't bother winning c4 back and grabs the centre instead.} 5... b5 {Hold on to the extra pawn.} 6. e5 {White chases the f6 knight.} 6... Nd5 {The knight lands on a strong central square, and no White pawn can attack it there.} *
